# Explain then annotate

When the user asks what a function, parameter, or block of code means, do both in the same turn:

1. Answer in chat.
2. Write the corresponding comments in the file being discussed.

Keep comments concise and in the same language the surrounding file already uses (this repo often uses Chinese). Explain non-obvious intent, ordering, or constraints — do not narrate obvious syntax. Do not wait for a follow-up "写注释".
